      "id": 1,
      "text": "Dixie, Georgia sits on the historic Dixie Highway, a road that once stretched from Canada all the way to Florida.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cobbcountycourier.com/2025/08/before-the-interstates-what-was-the-dixie-highway/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Good Roads Movement, sparked by cyclists and farmers in the 1870s, paved the way for Dixie’s early road improvements.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cobbcountycourier.com/2025/08/before-the-interstates-what-was-the-dixie-highway/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1921, Marietta issued a bond to pave roads leading into the city, reflecting the era’s focus on connectivity near Dixie.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cobbcountycourier.com/2025/08/before-the-interstates-what-was-the-dixie-highway/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the late 1920s, federal funds created a numbered highway system that replaced named routes like the Dixie Highway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cobbcountycourier.com/2025/08/before-the-interstates-what-was-the-dixie-highway/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "GDOT’s documentary on the Dixie Highway has earned positive reviews, sparking renewed interest in the corridor’s history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
